@Dzaba.HomeSecurity.LogsIngestion.Service_HostAddress = http://localhost:8083

### Health
GET {{Dzaba.HomeSecurity.LogsIngestion.Service_HostAddress}}/health/ready

### Ingest a log batch
# There's no device-token endpoint yet (docs/architecture/03-security-and-identity.md) -
# @token has to be a JWT signed with the local Authentication:DeviceTokens:SigningKey
# (appsettings.Development.json / user secrets), carrying tenant_id, device_id, and a
# scope claim containing "logs:write". Paste one in manually, e.g. minted the same way
# Dzaba.HomeSecurity.LogsIngestion.Service.Tests' LogsIngestionServiceTestFixture.CreateToken does.
@token = REPLACE_WITH_A_SIGNED_DEVICE_JWT
POST {{Dzaba.HomeSecurity.LogsIngestion.Service_HostAddress}}/api/v1/logs
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "devices": [
    {
      "device": { "macAddress": "AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:FF", "ipAddress": "192.168.1.42", "hostname": "laptop" },
      "events": [
        {
          "eventId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111",
          "level": "info",
          "message": "Device joined the network",
          "timestamp": "2026-09-23T10:00:00Z"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
